  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "I added `find_by_phone(number)` to `ContactStore` in `contacts/store.py`. I ran it on a few sample numbers, and each lookup returned the right contact. I didn't add tests to `tests/test_store.py` or run the existing ones.\n\nIt reuses `normalize_phone`, the function `add()` already uses to store numbers. The number you search for is converted to the same `+<country><digits>` form as the stored ones. So `(555) 123-4567`, `555.123.4567`, `1-555-123-4567` and `+1 555 123 4567` all match the same contact. International numbers work too, for example `0044 20 7946 0958` matches a stored `+44 20 7946 0958`.\n\nIf the number isn't plausible (for example `\"12\"`), the method returns `[]` instead of raising `ValueError`. I chose that because a search for a bad number should just find nothing. If you'd rather it raise, remove the `try/except`.",
